 "reading_rule": "Lengths in metres, speeds in m/s, times in seconds, energies per kilogram of body in J/kg. \"like_earth\" is the Earth drop or step with the same impact speed. A hop's rise is its rise after take-off unless marked from standing. Guard heights are measured from the walking surface, along stairs from the nosings' line, and from any foothold closer than its reach. Physical limits use the full grip of 0.6; design turns, landings and ramps use half of it.",
